      "snippet": {
        "text": "This direct link between these teachers' existing beliefs and their stance on adopting ChatGPT enriches the discourse on the uptake of educational technology, an aspect often glossed over in wider academic discussions. This relationship aligns with the TPACK framework as it considers how teachers' pedagogical approaches may influence their technology integration strategies (Mishra & Koehler, 2006;Mishra et al., 2023). \n\nIn terms of practical applications for student engagement, the present research suggests that most of the mathematics teachers in our study, intend to integrate Chat-GPT into their instructional techniques to improve their teaching. These approaches, related to the preparation of teaching materials, supporting students with specific needs and to engage students in discussion, offer tangible insights into the practical uses of ChatGPT in mathematics education that extend beyond the narratives of customisation and support highlighted in existing studies (Gill et al., 2024). The practical applications reported by these teachers direct us to the need for a balanced integration of technology, pedagogy, and content knowledge whereby teachers can create effective learning environments (Mishra & Koehler, 2006). \n\nFindings suggest that, while most of the teachers in our study perceive ChatGPT as a tool for change and improvement, their views seem more transactional rather than transformative. In other words, these teachers seem to consider ChatGPT as 'a sophisticated tool' that could help them do their work more efficiently. Hence, investigation into the more transformational advantages of utilising ChatGPT in mathematics learning, such as boosting student engagement and aiding in understanding complex mathematics concepts, becomes critical in our work to better understand how this technology can meet the distinctive objectives of mathematics education. Indeed, a more detailed and informed comprehension of ChatGPT's advantages about specific educational goals is seldom explored in the broader academic narratives.",
