ing, and problembased learning, etc.) that facilitate understanding.\n\n5. It is also recommended that teachers should use different problem-solving strategies (e.g.making systematic lists, and using similar simple problems, etc.).Students should also be encouraged to use these strategies.608 6.It seems useful to carry out research to investigate the possible causes of the lower mathematical understanding.The issues worth to study could be as follows: Running mathematics classes through presentation, group learning, the use or non-use of technology and materials in lessons, etc.",
