      "snippet": {
        "text": "In recent years, the educational landscape has witnessed a surge of interest in leveraging artificial intelligence (AI) tutor bots to revolutionize personalized instruction across various academic disciplines, such as mathematics learning (Lee & Yeo, 2022), foreign language learning (Kohnke et al., 2023;Mageira et al., 2022), science learning (Cooper, 2023), programming learning (Ahmed & Hasnine, 2023;Dos Santos & Cury, 2023;Yilmaz & Yilmaz, 2023), business education (Chen et al., 2023), and public health (Fadhil & Gabrielli, 2017;Lee et al., 2022). These intelligent chatbots, exemplified by platforms like ChatGPT, have emerged as tools for tailoring educational experiences to the unique needs of individual learners. \n\nAI chatbots or bots enabled by ChatGPT are conversational agents that utilize AI technologies to engage in interactive and dynamic conversations with users. Chat-GPT is a language model developed by OpenAI that is trained on a vast amount of text data from the internet (Wu et al., 2023). Since ChatGPT became publicly accessible in November 2022, various claims have been made about its advanced AI capabilities. These claims suggest that ChatGPT can engage students in real-time conversations, provide personalized guidance and support that is relevant and contextually appropriate, and adapt its interactions based on the specific needs and preferences of individual learners (Fadhil & Gabrielli, 2017;Zhai, 2022). \n\nThis paper proposes a framework for examining the personalization capabilities of current ChatGPT technologies, focusing on various levels of personalized learning (PL). It also presents an empirical study that investigates interactions between graduate students and a ChatGPT-based chatbot. In the remainder of this paper, we refer to this bot as a 'tutor bot' since it primarily serves that role. Fifty-one graduate students participated in one-on-one tutoring sessions with the bot, focusing on the topic of educational reforms. These conversations were recorded and analyzed. \n\nThe study examines how effectively the tutor bot created individualized learning experiences for students, tailoring interactions to their unique needs and helping them articulate a deeper understanding of the topic.",
